---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Shahid Tasbih - Aerospace Engineer">
  <div class="layout">
    <Sidebar />

    <main class="content">

      <!-- ABOUT -->
      <section id="about" class="section">
        <h3 class="section-heading-mobile">About</h3>
        <div class="about-text">
          <p>
            I'm an aerospace engineering student in
            <a href="https://aeroastro.mit.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT's Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics</a>
            (Course 16), driven by a fascination with what lies beyond our atmosphere. My work sits at the
            intersection of <span class="highlight">autonomous systems</span>,
            <span class="highlight">machine learning</span>, and
            <span class="highlight">spacecraft design</span>.
          </p>
          <p>
            I've always been the kind of person who dives headfirst into challenges just to see what
            happens. In high school, I built a giant ninja star out of 256 sheets of paper for my
            Geometry class, starting from 1, then 4, 16, 64, 256, only stopping because my teacher
            ran out of unused packets. I taught myself AP Calc AB and BC in two weeks just because
            Precalc wasn't challenging enough. I finished every AP World History chapter over
            Thanksgiving break on a whim. The worst that can happen is I fail, and learn something
            new in the process.
          </p>
          <p>
            That same mindset drives my work today. I'm passionate about building autonomous machines
            that can perceive and navigate complex environments, from lunar landers that teach
            themselves to touch down safely, to robotic systems and prediction models that operate
            under real-world constraints. Beyond autonomy, I'm deeply interested in the propulsion
            systems that will take us further: designing future spacecraft capable of covering vast
            interstellar distances in short times, potentially through
            <span class="highlight">nuclear propulsion</span> technologies.
          </p>
          <p>
            Right now, I'm a research assistant in MIT's AeroAstro department, working on flight
            software for satellite systems and optimizing orbital event detection with neural networks
            on embedded hardware. When I'm not in the lab, I'm usually training reinforcement learning
            agents, building hardware, or iterating on side projects that scratch a curiosity itch.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="note">
          <span class="note-label">For students reading this</span>
          <p>
            You don't need permission to start. Every project here began with me being curious
            and a little bored: teaching myself Calc BC in two weeks, building an AC out of
            scrap and aluminum foil, training an agent to land on the Moon. Pick something that
            scares you a little and start badly. The worst case is you fail and learn something,
            which is a pretty good worst case.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- EXPERIENCE -->
      <section id="experience" class="section">
        <h3 class="section-heading-mobile">Experience</h3>

        <Card
          period="Jan 2026 - May 2026"
          title="Research Assistant · MIT AeroAstro"
          description="Utilized the F Prime framework to compile and execute flight software on the RP2350 chip for satellite applications. Currently conducting a comparative analysis between CNNs and algorithmic methods on NVIDIA Jetson Nano to optimize orbital event detection under strict power and memory constraints."
          href="https://aeroastro.mit.edu/"
          tags={[
            { label: "F Prime", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F_Prime" },
            { label: "CNNs", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convolutional_neural_network" },
            { label: "Jetson Nano", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nvidia_Jetson" },
            { label: "Python", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Python_(programming_language)" },
            { label: "Embedded Systems", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embedded_system" },
          ]}
        />

        <a class="resume-link" href="/assets/resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          View Full Résumé
          <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- PROJECTS -->
      <section id="projects" class="section">
        <h3 class="section-heading-mobile">Projects</h3>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/lunar-lander">
          <div class="card-period">Reinforcement Learning</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              Deep Q-Network for Autonomous Lunar Landing
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              Engineered a PyTorch D3QN agent to solve a 2D landing environment with &gt;95% success,
              then extended into a custom 3D rigid-body MuJoCo simulation with accurate 1.62 m/s²
              lunar gravity. Upgraded to DDPG for a 13-dimensional continuous state space with a
              hybrid PD-RL attitude controller mapping actions across 5 thrusters.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <a class="tag" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PyTorch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PyTorch</a>
              <a class="tag" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Q-learning#Deep_Q-network" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D3QN</a>
              <a class="tag" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deterministic_policy_gradient" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DDPG</a>
              <a class="tag" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MuJoCo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MuJoCo</a>
              <a class="tag" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Experience_replay" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PER</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/ufo">
          <div class="card-period">G-Force Mitigation</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              UFO Project
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              Building a centrifugal system that cancels linear acceleration via rotational
              mechanics, aimed at aggressive jet and missile-evasion maneuvers without the same
              sustained load on a pilot. A 2D RL policy cuts a 10g outer pulse down to ~1.64g
              on the inner accelerometer.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <span class="tag">RL</span>
              <span class="tag">Simulation</span>
              <span class="tag">Controls</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/6-axis-arm">
          <div class="card-period">Robotics</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              6-Axis Arm
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              Adaptive inverse kinematics that keeps learning through hardware deformities
              using a Hebbian control policy, so everyday IK can tolerate looser (cheaper)
              mechanical tolerances instead of perfect calibration forever.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <span class="tag">Hebbian</span>
              <span class="tag">IK</span>
              <span class="tag">MuJoCo</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/kalshi-optimization">
          <div class="card-period">Markets + ML</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              Kalshi Optimization
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              Autonomous sports-contract scanner that fuses Elo, bookmaker odds, and team
              stats into a fair-value model, then sizes edges with Kelly under statistical-mechanics
              risk dampers and Telegram alerts.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <span class="tag">Elo</span>
              <span class="tag">Kelly</span>
              <span class="tag">Kalshi</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/spike-detector">
          <div class="card-period">ML + Markets</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              Spike Detector
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              Pre-market binary classifier for significant intraday moves: two-stage XGBoost
              with FinBERT sentiment and a stat-mech layer, fully automated paper trading via
              Alpaca and Telegram.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <span class="tag">XGBoost</span>
              <span class="tag">FinBERT</span>
              <span class="tag">Alpaca</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="/projects/erwin">
          <div class="card-period">AI Voice</div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <h4 class="card-title">
              Project Erwin
              <svg class="card-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7" /><path d="M7 7h10v10" />
              </svg>
            </h4>
            <p class="card-description">
              AI secretary that schedules, reminds, and commands from your Obsidian vault,
              speaking as Commander Erwin via ElevenLabs-trained weights deployed on Piper TTS.
            </p>
            <div class="card-tags">
              <span class="tag">Voice AI</span>
              <span class="tag">Obsidian</span>
              <span class="tag">Piper</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- COMMUNITY -->
      <section id="community" class="section">
        <h3 class="section-heading-mobile">Community</h3>

        <Card
          period="STEM Education"
          title="RiseEd · Accessible STEM Learning"
          description="Built RiseEd to make STEM approachable for younger students, especially those from low-income backgrounds. Designed a website of simple, engaging lesson slides and booklets, iterating on feedback from teachers to turn intimidating topics into resources students and educators could actually use."
          tags={[
            { label: "Education" },
            { label: "Outreach" },
            { label: "Curriculum Design" },
            { label: "Web" },
          ]}
        />

        <Card
          period="Thermodynamics"
          title="CoolBreeze · Low-Cost Air Conditioner"
          description="Designed and built a low-cost air conditioner grounded in thermodynamics principles, optimizing insulation and efficiency on a tight budget, then documented the full build in a video to make the science reproducible for anyone who wanted to follow along."
          tags={[
            { label: "Thermodynamics" },
            { label: "Hardware" },
            { label: "DIY" },
            { label: "Science Comm" },
          ]}
        />
      </section>

      <!-- EDUCATION -->
      <section id="education" class="section">
        <h3 class="section-heading-mobile">Education</h3>

        <Card
          period="June 2025 - June 2029"
          title="Massachusetts Institute of Technology"
          description="Candidate for B.S. in Aerospace Engineering (Course 16). <br /><strong>Relevant Coursework:</strong> Introduction to Autonomy <br /><strong>Advanced Learning (Audit):</strong> Deep Learning (Graduate Level), Advances in Computer Vision (Graduate Level)"
          tags={[]}
        />

        <Card
          period="Sep 2023 - Apr 2024"
          title="The Coding School"
          description="Completed two-semester courses in Artificial Intelligence and Quantum Computing, developing neural network, NLP, and reinforcement learning models for real-world applications. Implemented foundational quantum algorithms using the Cirq library."
          tags={[]}
        />
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
    const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section');
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          const id = entry.target.getAttribute('id');
          navLinks.forEach((link) => {
            link.classList.toggle('active', link.getAttribute('data-section') === id);
          });
        }
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -60% 0px', threshold: 0 });
    sections.forEach((s) => observer.observe(s));
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
